        "Heino Falcke",
        "Sheperd S. Doeleman"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Horizon-scale black-hole imaging is a singular observational achievement, bringing strong-field gravity into direct empirical view.",
        "attribution": "Falcke articulated the imaging opportunity and Doeleman led the observational realization; the collaboration's scale makes individual credit necessarily incomplete.",
        "maturity": "Multiple EHT results and independent analyses have made this a mature, durable result.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The proper allocation of credit among the many instrumental and collaboration leaders remains difficult."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 2,
      "ballot_id": "B029",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Daniel J. Eisenstein",
        "Shaun Cole"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BAO transformed relic early-universe physics into a robust cosmological distance ruler with profound leverage on cosmic expansion.",
        "attribution": "Eisenstein and Cole are central to the observational establishment, though the theoretical and survey contributions were broadly distributed.",
        "maturity": "The signal has been repeatedly confirmed and is now a standard component of precision cosmology.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Attribution across theory, survey design, and analysis communities is intrinsically broad."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
      "ballot_id": "B026",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Francis Halzen",
        "Christian Spiering"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "IceCube opened high-energy neutrino astronomy and supplied compelling evidence for an extragalactic neutrino flux.",
        "attribution": "Halzen and Spiering were key scientific and institutional leaders, while the accomplishment rests on a large collaboration.",
        "maturity": "The astrophysical flux and source associations have accumulated over more than a decade.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Individual source populations and the relative credit among IceCube founders require careful review."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 4,
      "ballot_id": "B053",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Charles L. Bennett",
        "David N. Spergel",
        "Lyman A. Page"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "WMAP's precision map made the standard cosmological description quantitatively testable and broadly persuasive.",
        "attribution": "These figures represent leadership in mission, interpretation, and measurement, but the scientific output was collective.",
        "maturity": "Its principal conclusions have endured stringent comparison with later CMB observations.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Separating WMAP's independent contribution from subsequent Planck precision is not straightforward."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "ballot_id": "B001",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Brian D. Metzger",
        "Daniel Kasen",
        "Masaomi Tanaka"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Kilonova observations connected neutron-star mergers to heavy-element production in a striking multi-messenger confirmation.",
        "attribution": "Metzger, Kasen, and Tanaka made major contributions to the theoretical interpretation, although observational and gravitational-wave contributors are also indispensable.",
        "maturity": "The 2017 event was transformative and later observations support the framework, but the sample remains limited.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The quantitative share of r-process elements made in mergers remains unsettled.",
          "The candidate list emphasizes interpretation more than the observational discovery."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 6,
      "ballot_id": "B009",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "David Charbonneau",
        "William J. Borucki"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Transit measurements made exoplanet detection scalable and converted a remarkable discovery into a population science.",
        "attribution": "Charbonneau's early detection and Borucki's Kepler leadership are clear landmarks; the method has many precursors and contributors.",
        "maturity": "The transit method has been decisively validated by extensive discoveries and atmospheric follow-up.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Credit must be distinguished carefully from the earlier discovery of exoplanets already recognized by the Prize."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 7,
      "ballot_id": "B058",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Hidetoshi Katori",
        "Jun Ye"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical lattice clocks have produced a major advance in timekeeping and precision tests of fundamental physics.",
        "attribution": "Katori and Ye are the clearest leading figures in invention and realization.",
        "maturity": "Performance, reproducibility, and scientific applications have been demonstrated across laboratories for many years.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The ultimate foundational and practical consequences are still developing."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 8,
      "ballot_id": "B038",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Alan H. Guth",
        "Andrei Linde",
        "Viatcheslav Mukhanov"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Inflation and the quantum account of primordial structure are among the most consequential frameworks in modern cosmology.",
        "attribution": "Guth, Linde, and Mukhanov represent distinct foundational elements, although the historical development is extensive.",
        "maturity": "CMB observations strongly support key predictions, yet do not uniquely establish a particular inflationary mechanism.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "No direct evidence identifies the inflationary dynamics or separates inflation uniquely from alternatives.",
          "The appropriate attribution among many theoretical contributors remains contested."
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
